        "evidence": "md:14-18 'this class {K: g(K)≤4} is generated from a finite list of torus-knot generators plus skein crossing changes'; md:30-40 'Every Bring-embeddable knot is obtained from the seven torus-knot generators by skein crossing changes'",
        "notes": "The set {K : g(K) ≤ 4} is INFINITE (infinitely many distinct knots have Seifert genus ≤ 4), so 'a finite list of generators' generating it requires the skein-crossing-change closure to be doing all the work — but skein crossing changes do not preserve genus (md:40 itself hedges 'when chosen in the principled atlas methodology'). As stated, 'finite list of generators generates {g≤4}' is at best unproven and at face value false; it is propped on prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete without an in-block argument."
